"For each item below, fetch its source and check that the recorded quote appears on the page and supports the item. A card item is a field of the plan in the producer's words, with the sources it cites: check each factual claim in it against those sources, and any value it carries against the page; what the plan will build, measure or predict needs no source, but a factual claim with no source is UNSUPPORTED. For a cost input, check that the page states the number for the setting given; whether it applies to this plan is not yours to judge. When the page states a different number for a num or rate item, give it as page_value. Decide only from the pages you fetch and the text below; do not read files. Return one status per item, under its ref: SUPPORTED, PARTIAL, UNSUPPORTED, CONTRADICTED or UNREACHABLE, with the page sentence you relied on.
Items, one per line:
{\"ref\":\"card:question\",\"text\":\"Does increasing the capacity of a neural ingredient-substitution model measurably improve its ranking of sustainable replacements, measured as Hit@1 on Recipe1MSubs [src_gismo_sizes]?\",\"sources\":[{\"id\":\"src_gismo_sizes\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2302.07960v1\",\"quote\":\"we get 49,044, 10,729 and 10,747 substitution samples for training, validation, and test sets respectively.\"}]}
{\"ref\":\"card:hypothesis\",\"text\":\"More capacity in a substitution ranker improves substitution ranking because larger encoders capture finer ingredient context, as LLM results suggest [src_llm].\",\"sources\":[{\"id\":\"src_llm\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2409.08792\",\"quote\":\"Our approach improved Hit@1 accuracy on ingredient substitution tasks, from the baseline 34.53 ± 0.10% to 38.03 ± 0.28% on the original GISMo dataset, and from 40.24 ± 0.36% to 54.46 ± 0.29% on a refined version of the same dataset.\"}]}
{\"ref\":\"card:if_lever\",\"text\":\"Hit@1 rises with width, reaching at least 22 percent at width 512, above GISMo's 20.56, and still climbing.\",\"sources\":[]}
{\"ref\":\"card:if_not\",\"text\":\"Hit@1 plateaus near GISMo's 20.56 at every width; extra capacity adds nothing, so wider models are not the lever.\",\"sources\":[]}
{\"ref\":\"card:test_summary\",\"text\":\"Reproduce GISMo's Recipe1MSubs result, then train the ranker at four widths 64, 128, 256, 512 with five seeds each on four GPUs; if Hit@1 climbs past the 20.56 baseline with width, compute is the lever.\",\"sources\":[]}
{\"ref\":\"card:closest_prior\",\"text\":\"Rita 2024 fine-tuned GPT-3.5 and TinyLlama on Recipe1MSubs, lifting Hit@1 from 34.53 to 38.03; no capacity sweep within one protocol exists [src_llm].\",\"sources\":[{\"id\":\"src_llm\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2409.08792\",\"quote\":\"Our approach improved Hit@1 accuracy on ingredient substitution tasks, from the baseline 34.53 ± 0.10% to 38.03 ± 0.28% on the original GISMo dataset, and from 40.24 ± 0.36% to 54.46 ± 0.29% on a refined version of the same dataset.\"}]}
{\"ref\":\"card:left_open\",\"text\":\"Whether ranking quality keeps rising with model capacity inside one fixed protocol on Recipe1MSubs is unmeasured; the only scaling evidence is cross-protocol.\",\"sources\":[]}
{\"ref\":\"card:anchor\",\"text\":\"Reproduce GISMo's published test-set MRR of 31.51 and Hit@1 of 20.56 using the official code, within 2 MRR points [src_gismo_gismo].\",\"sources\":[{\"id\":\"src_gismo_gismo\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2302.07960v1\",\"quote\":\"GISMo (Ours) 31.51±0.10 20.56±0.14 35.89±0.16 54.27±0.19\"}],\"value\":31.51}
{\"ref\":\"card:limits\",\"text\":\"Shows ranking accuracy on home recipes, not industrial formulations, and never measures actual environmental footprint or sensory quality of the substitute.\",\"sources\":[]}
{\"ref\":\"src:src_gismo_sizes\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2302.07960v1\",\"quote\":\"we get 49,044, 10,729 and 10,747 substitution samples for training, validation, and test sets respectively.\",\"supports\":\"Recipe1MSubs split sizes used by the plan\"}
{\"ref\":\"src:src_llm\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2409.08792\",\"quote\":\"Our approach improved Hit@1 accuracy on ingredient substitution tasks, from the baseline 34.53 ± 0.10% to 38.03 ± 0.28% on the original GISMo dataset, and from 40.24 ± 0.36% to 54.46 ± 0.29% on a refined version of the same dataset.\",\"supports\":\"the closest prior and the direction that larger models help\"}
